      "text": "To solve the given expression \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\), we need to first recognize the pattern and simplify the expression step by step.\n\n1. **Identify the Pattern:**\n   The expression alternates between positive and negative terms. The first term is positive, the second term is negative, and so on. The sequence of positive terms is \\(1, 7, 13, \\ldots, 49, 55\\) and the sequence of negative terms is \\(-4, -10, -16, \\ldots, -46\\).\n\n2. **Express the Sequence Mathematically:**\n   The sequence of positive terms can be described as \\(a_n = 3n - 2\\) for \\(n = 1, 2, \\ldots, 19\\).\n   The sequence of negative terms can be described as \\(b_n = -4n\\) for \\(n = 1, 2, \\ldots, 13\\).\n\n3. **Sum the Positive Terms:**\n   The sum of the positive terms is:\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{n=1}^{19} (3n - 2)\n   \\]\n   This can be split into two sums:\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{n=1}^{19} 3n - \\sum_{n=1}^{19} 2 = 3 \\sum_{n=1}^{19} n - 2 \\sum_{n=1}^{19} 1\n   \\]\n   Using the formulas for the sum of the first \\(n\\) natural numbers and the sum of a constant, we get:\n   \\[\n   3 \\cdot \\frac{19 \\cdot 20}{2} - 2 \\cdot 19 = 3 \\cdot 190 - 38 = 570 - 38 = 532\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the Negative Terms:**\n   The sum of the negative terms is:\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{n=1}^{13} (-4n) = -4 \\sum_{n=1}^{13} n = -4 \\cdot \\frac{13 \\cdot 14}{2} = -4 \\cdot 91 = -364\n   \\]\n\n5. **Combine the Results:**\n   The total sum of the expression is the sum of the positive terms minus the sum of the negative terms:\n   \\[\n   532 - (-364) = 532 + 364 = 900\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is \\(\\boxed{900}\\).",
