      "text": "To solve the expression \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\), we need to identify the pattern and then sum the series.\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the expression to see if we can identify any pattern:\n\\[1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55.\\]\n\nWe observe that the series alternates between adding and subtracting terms. Let's group the terms in pairs:\n\\[(1 - 4) + (7 - 10) + (13 - 16) + \\cdots + (49 - 52) + 55.\\]\n\nNow, let's calculate the value of each pair:\n\\[1 - 4 = -3,\\]\n\\[7 - 10 = -3,\\]\n\\[13 - 16 = -3,\\]\n\\[\\cdots,\\]\n\\[49 - 52 = -3.\\]\n\nThere are 11 pairs in the sequence, and each pair sums to \\(-3\\). Therefore, the sum of the 11 pairs is:\n\\[-3 \\times 11 = -33.\\]\n\nWe also need to add the last term, which is \\(55\\), to this sum:\n\\[-33 + 55 = 22.\\]\n\nThus, the value of the expression is:\n\\[\\boxed{22}.\\]",
